      "ai": {
        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add desktop.turnstalled telemetry event",
        "summary": "New desktop.turn_stalled event fires when a turn produces no harness stream activity for the configured window. Telemetry only; does not abort the turn. Added to ALWAYS_TRACK_EVENTS in common/src/util/analytics-sampling.ts to ensure rare reliability signals are never sampled. Join with desktop.turn_completed to distinguish recovered long-silent tool calls from real hangs.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T15:34:44.414Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "If the assistant stops making visible progress for a while during a task, the system now quietly records a 'turn stalled' event. This only adds a monitoring signal; it does not interrupt or cancel the task, so nothing you see changes. The developer comment notes this helps distinguish a long-silent tool call that later recovers from a true hang when reviewing completed turns.",
