        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add affiliate signup and activation analytics events",
        "summary": "Added `FREEBUFF_AFFILIATE_SIGNUP` and `FREEBUFF_AFFILIATE_ACTIVATION` to `AnalyticsEvent` enum in `common/src/constants/analytics-events.ts`. These events track affiliate-driven user acquisition and activation funnels. Scope limited to shared core constants. Event strings map to `freebuff.affiliate.signup` and `freebuff.affiliate.activation`.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T15:34:45.795Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The product now records two new analytics events when someone signs up or activates through an affiliate link, so the tracking system can tell which users came from affiliate recommendations versus other sources. If you looked at the analytics dashboard, you would see new funnel steps labeled affiliate signup and affiliate activation appearing alongside the existing acquisition events. This change is in place now, but it only adds the ability to capture these events, so you would not notice anything different until the affiliate program starts sending users through tracked links and the team begins reporting on the new data.",
